<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.1.1: Understanding Value</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00051</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.1.1: Understanding Value</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9cb229d9-e088-406f-86d8-23b14444af58</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Here are some letters and what they represent. All costs are in dollars.</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represents the cost of a main dish.</item>
        <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represents the number of side dishes.</item>
        <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>s</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represents the cost of a side dish.</item>
        <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represents the total cost of a meal.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00002">For questions 1 - 4, discuss what each <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">equation</term> means with a partner. Then, describe the situation in words.</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7.50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00005">A main dish costs $7.50.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>s</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4.50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00008">Your answer may vary, but here are some examples.</para>
          <list id="list-00002">
            <item>The cost of a main dish is the cost of the side dish plus $4.50.</item>
            <item>The cost of a main dish is $4.50 more than the cost of a side dish.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mi>s</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00011">The number of side dishes times the cost of the side dish is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00012"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mi>s</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00014">The main dish added to the quantity of the number of side dishes times the cost of the side dish represents the total cost of the meal.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00015">Write a new equation that could be true in this same situation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00017">Your answer may vary, but here are some examples.</para>
          <list id="list-00003">
            <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
            <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>s</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4.5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
            <item><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>13.5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00018">Describe what your new equation means in words.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00020">Your answer may vary, but here are some examples.</para>
          <list id="list-00004">
            <item>The main dish costs <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item>The difference in cost between the main dish and a side dish is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>4.50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>13.50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is the cost of the main dish and a <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>$</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> tip.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>